@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ocar-nouns`

-- TEST FIXTURES for the O-Car encoding: named cases, and helpers that build them. No rule and
-- no directive is here; the tests modules import this one.
--
-- Every figure here is a SCENARIO VALUE, chosen to make the arithmetic visible: a sum insured of
-- 600,000,000, a premium of 12,000,000, a loss on Wednesday 10 June 2026. None is a figure the
-- document prints; the figures the document prints are asserted in the tests, each beside its
-- source line.
--
-- The nouns ask the caller for every fact, with no default. These helpers are a TEST convenience
-- only: a fact not named in the list a helper is given is taken as absent. They are not part of
-- what an API caller sees.

§ `Test fixtures`

§§ `The vehicle`

GIVEN `the origin`                IS A `The origin of the vehicle`
      `new when insured`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `first registered`          IS A DATE
      `made in`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the use`                   IS A `A use that raises depreciation`
GIVETH A `The vehicle`
`a car` `the origin` `, new:` `new when insured` `, first registered` `first registered` `, made in` `made in` `, used as` `the use` MEANS
    `The vehicle` WITH
        `number of wheels`                                          IS 4
        `runs on rails`                                             IS FALSE
        `a two- or three-wheeled motorcycle or a similar vehicle`   IS FALSE
        `origin`                                                    IS `the origin`
        `new (100%) when insured`                                   IS `new when insured`
        `date of first registration in Vietnam`                     IS `first registered`
        `year of manufacture`                                       IS `made in`
        `use`                                                       IS `the use`
        `carries`                                                   IS `passengers`
        `permitted load in the inspection certificate`              IS 1000
        `permitted number of persons in the inspection certificate` IS 5

-- A private five-seat car made in Vietnam, first registered 15 March 2022: on a contract made
-- in January 2026 its time in use is 46 months (1.15).
`the private car` MEANS
    `a car` `manufactured in Vietnam` `, new:` FALSE `, first registered` (YMD 2022 3 15) `, made in` 2022 `, used as` `none of the uses listed in 14.1.2(b)`

GIVEN `carries what` IS A `What the vehicle carries`
      `permitted load` IS A NUMBER
      `permitted persons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The vehicle`
`a vehicle carrying` `carries what` `, permitted load` `permitted load` `, permitted persons` `permitted persons` MEANS
    `The vehicle` WITH
        `number of wheels`                                          IS 4
        `runs on rails`                                             IS FALSE
        `a two- or three-wheeled motorcycle or a similar vehicle`   IS FALSE
        `origin`                                                    IS `manufactured in Vietnam`
        `new (100%) when insured`                                   IS FALSE
        `date of first registration in Vietnam`                     IS YMD 2022 3 15
        `year of manufacture`                                       IS 2022
        `use`                                                       IS `none of the uses listed in 14.1.2(b)`
        `carries`                                                   IS `carries what`
        `permitted load in the inspection certificate`              IS `permitted load`
        `permitted number of persons in the inspection certificate` IS `permitted persons`

§§ `The supplementary clauses`

GIVEN c IS A `A supplementary clause`
GIVETH A `A supplementary clause on the policy`
`clause accepted and paid in full and on time:` c MEANS
    `A supplementary clause on the policy` WITH
        `clause`                            IS c
        `accepted by the Insurer`           IS TRUE
        `premium paid in full`              IS TRUE
        `premium paid on time`              IS TRUE
        `sub-limit in the contract`         IS NOTHING
        `benefit limit in the contract`     IS NOTHING
        `deductible otherwise agreed`       IS NOTHING
        `number of losses otherwise agreed` IS NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A supplementary clause`
GIVETH A `A supplementary clause on the policy`
`clause accepted and paid in full but late:` c MEANS
    `A supplementary clause on the policy` WITH
        `clause`                            IS c
        `accepted by the Insurer`           IS TRUE
        `premium paid in full`              IS TRUE
        `premium paid on time`              IS FALSE
        `sub-limit in the contract`         IS NOTHING
        `benefit limit in the contract`     IS NOTHING
        `deductible otherwise agreed`       IS NOTHING
        `number of losses otherwise agreed` IS NOTHING

GIVEN `the sub-limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A supplementary clause on the policy`
`BS04 with a sub-limit of` `the sub-limit` MEANS
    `A supplementary clause on the policy` WITH
        `clause`                            IS `BS04 settlement up to a limit of liability`
        `accepted by the Insurer`           IS TRUE
        `premium paid in full`              IS TRUE
        `premium paid on time`              IS TRUE
        `sub-limit in the contract`         IS JUST `the sub-limit`
        `benefit limit in the contract`     IS NOTHING
        `deductible otherwise agreed`       IS NOTHING
        `number of losses otherwise agreed` IS NOTHING

GIVEN `the limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A supplementary clause on the policy`
`BS06 with a limit of` `the limit` MEANS
    `A supplementary clause on the policy` WITH
        `clause`                            IS `BS06 safe journey`
        `accepted by the Insurer`           IS TRUE
        `premium paid in full`              IS TRUE
        `premium paid on time`              IS TRUE
        `sub-limit in the contract`         IS NOTHING
        `benefit limit in the contract`     IS JUST `the limit`
        `deductible otherwise agreed`       IS NOTHING
        `number of losses otherwise agreed` IS NOTHING

§§ `The policy`

-- A policy for the calendar year 2026, concluded 1 January 2026, sum insured 600,000,000, with
-- the vehicle, the market value, the supplementary clauses and the contract date as given.
GIVEN v                 IS A `The vehicle`
      `concluded on`    IS A DATE
      `the sum insured` IS A NUMBER
      `the market value` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the clauses`     IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause on the policy`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`a 2026 policy on` v `, concluded on` `concluded on` `, insured for` `the sum insured` `, market value` `the market value` `, with` `the clauses` MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `vehicle`                                                         IS v
        `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS `concluded on`
        `start of the insurance period`                                   IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `last day of the insurance period`                                IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `sum insured`                                                     IS `the sum insured`
        `market value when insured`                                       IS `the market value`
        `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS 800_000_000
        `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS NOTHING
        `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS NOTHING
        `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS NOTHING
        `premium`                                                         IS 12_000_000
        `premium paid`                                                    IS 12_000_000
        `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 15
        `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS FALSE
        `supplementary clauses`                                           IS `the clauses`
        `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS EMPTY
        `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS TRUE
        `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS TRUE

GIVEN `the clauses` IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause on the policy`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the 2026 policy with` `the clauses` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy on` `the private car` `, concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, insured for` 600_000_000 `, market value` (JUST 600_000_000) `, with` `the clauses`

-- The plain policy: no supplementary clause, insured at its market value.
`the plain policy` MEANS `the 2026 policy with` EMPTY

-- The same car insured for 400,000,000 against a market value of 600,000,000.
GIVEN `the clauses` IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause on the policy`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the under-insured policy with` `the clauses` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy on` `the private car` `, concluded on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, insured for` 400_000_000 `, market value` (JUST 600_000_000) `, with` `the clauses`

-- Variants on the premium, the deductible and the contract's own figures.
GIVEN `the deductible` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the reduction level` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `paid` IS A NUMBER
      `owed allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `others` IS A LIST OF `Another policy on the vehicle`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the plain policy with deductible` `the deductible` `, reduction level` `the reduction level` `, premium paid` `paid` `, owing allowed` `owed allowed` `, other policies` `others` MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `vehicle`                                                         IS `the private car`
        `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `start of the insurance period`                                   IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `last day of the insurance period`                                IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `sum insured`                                                     IS 600_000_000
        `market value when insured`                                       IS JUST 600_000_000
        `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS 800_000_000
        `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS NOTHING
        `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS `the deductible`
        `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS `the reduction level`
        `premium`                                                         IS 12_000_000
        `premium paid`                                                    IS `paid`
        `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 15
        `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS `owed allowed`
        `supplementary clauses`                                           IS EMPTY
        `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS `others`
        `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS TRUE
        `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS TRUE

-- Variants on the insurance period (for BS05's limit by the length of the contract).
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the last day`  IS A DATE
      `the clauses`   IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause on the policy`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`a policy from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` `, with` `the clauses` MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `vehicle`                                                         IS `the private car`
        `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS `the first day`
        `start of the insurance period`                                   IS `the first day`
        `last day of the insurance period`                                IS `the last day`
        `sum insured`                                                     IS 600_000_000
        `market value when insured`                                       IS JUST 600_000_000
        `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS 800_000_000
        `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS NOTHING
        `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS NOTHING
        `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS NOTHING
        `premium`                                                         IS 12_000_000
        `premium paid`                                                    IS 12_000_000
        `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS `the first day`
        `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS FALSE
        `supplementary clauses`                                           IS `the clauses`
        `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS EMPTY
        `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS TRUE
        `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS TRUE

-- Variants on the valuation (13.2): the market value not determined, a customs rate.
GIVEN v IS A `The vehicle`
      `the customs rate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The policy`
`a policy with no market value on` v `, customs rate` `the customs rate` MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `vehicle`                                                         IS v
        `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `start of the insurance period`                                   IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `last day of the insurance period`                                IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `sum insured`                                                     IS 400_000_000
        `market value when insured`                                       IS NOTHING
        `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS 800_000_000
        `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS `the customs rate`
        `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS NOTHING
        `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS NOTHING
        `premium`                                                         IS 12_000_000
        `premium paid`                                                    IS 12_000_000
        `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 15
        `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS FALSE
        `supplementary clauses`                                           IS EMPTY
        `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS EMPTY
        `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS TRUE
        `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS TRUE

§§ `The circumstances of the loss`

-- The boolean facts of `The circumstances of the loss`, one member each, so that a test can say
-- which hold. Test-only.
DECLARE `A circumstance in a test` IS ONE OF
    `fact 12.1 deliberately caused`
    `fact 11.1 the malicious act was by an interested person`
    `fact not in traffic`
    `fact 12.3 no licence is required`
    `fact 12.4 over the alcohol limit`
    `fact 12.4 drugs`
    `fact 12.5 prohibited manoeuvre`
    `fact 12.6 prohibited parking`
    `fact 12.7 driving practice`
    `fact 12.7 driving practice agreed`
    `fact 12.7 racing`
    `fact 12.7 unlawful towing`
    `fact 12.8 unlawful carriage of goods`
    `fact 12.9 outside Vietnam`
    `fact 12.10 war or riot`
    `fact 12.16 fraud or abuse of trust`
    `fact 12.17 own special equipment`
    `fact 12.22 proven untruthful`
    `fact 12.22 important information omitted`
    `fact 12.22 the omission was inadvertent`
    `fact 12.24 not re-inspected`

GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `The inspection certificate`
      `the licence` IS A `The driving licence`
      fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance in a test`
GIVETH A `The circumstances of the loss`
`the circumstances, certificate` `the certificate` `, licence` `the licence` `, with` fs MEANS
    `The circumstances of the loss` WITH
        `deliberately caused by the Policyholder, the Owner, the Driver or a person with an interest in the vehicle` IS elem `fact 12.1 deliberately caused` fs
        `the malicious act was by the Policyholder, the Insured, the Owner, the Driver or a person with an interest in the vehicle` IS elem `fact 11.1 the malicious act was by an interested person` fs
        `in traffic`                                                  IS NOT elem `fact not in traffic` fs
        `inspection certificate`                                      IS `the certificate`
        `driving licence`                                             IS `the licence`
        `a licence is required for this type of vehicle`              IS NOT elem `fact 12.3 no licence is required` fs
        `the Driver was over the legal alcohol limit`                 IS elem `fact 12.4 over the alcohol limit` fs
        `the Driver had used drugs or prohibited stimulants`          IS elem `fact 12.4 drugs` fs
        `a prohibited manoeuvre listed in 12.5`                       IS elem `fact 12.5 prohibited manoeuvre` fs
        `stopped or parked where prohibited, leading to the damage`   IS elem `fact 12.6 prohibited parking` fs
        `used for driving practice`                                   IS elem `fact 12.7 driving practice` fs
        `driving practice was agreed`                                 IS elem `fact 12.7 driving practice agreed` fs
        `used for racing`                                             IS elem `fact 12.7 racing` fs
        `towing another vehicle unlawfully`                           IS elem `fact 12.7 unlawful towing` fs
        `carrying goods unlawfully or without the loading safety rules` IS elem `fact 12.8 unlawful carriage of goods` fs
        `in Vietnam`                                                  IS NOT elem `fact 12.9 outside Vietnam` fs
        `war, terrorism, civil war, strike or riot`                   IS elem `fact 12.10 war or riot` fs
        `total loss by fraud or abuse of trust`                       IS elem `fact 12.16 fraud or abuse of trust` fs
        `caused by the vehicle's own special-purpose equipment`       IS elem `fact 12.17 own special equipment` fs
        `claim information proven by the Insurer untruthful or forged` IS elem `fact 12.22 proven untruthful` fs
        `important information omitted`                               IS elem `fact 12.22 important information omitted` fs
        `the omission was inadvertent`                                IS elem `fact 12.22 the omission was inadvertent` fs
        `overhauled, modified or converted and not yet re-inspected`   IS elem `fact 12.24 not re-inspected` fs

GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance in a test`
GIVETH A `The circumstances of the loss`
`the circumstances with` fs MEANS
    `the circumstances, certificate` `valid and in force` `, licence` `a valid licence appropriate to the vehicle` `, with` fs

§§ `The conduct after the loss`

DECLARE `A conduct in a test` IS ONE OF
    `conduct force majeure`
    `conduct assessed within 5 days`
    `conduct hotline told`
    `conduct mitigation not taken`
    `conduct police not told`
    `conduct Insurer not told at once`
    `conduct instructions not followed`
    `conduct parked on a slope`
    `conduct dismantled without approval`
    `conduct Insurer silent 5 working days`
    `conduct scene not protected`
    `conduct necessary`
    `conduct claim against third party not preserved`
    `conduct untruthful`
    `conduct use misdeclared`
    `conduct increase in risk not notified`

GIVEN `notified on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `premium due` IS A NUMBER
      cs IS A LIST OF `A conduct in a test`
GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`the conduct, notified on` `notified on` `, premium that should have been paid` `premium due` `, where` cs MEANS
    `The conduct after the loss` WITH
        `date the Insurer was notified of the loss`                       IS `notified on`
        `force majeure prevented notice`                                  IS elem `conduct force majeure` cs
        `the Insurer assessed the damage within those 5 days`             IS elem `conduct assessed within 5 days` cs
        `the hotline was told at the time of the accident`                IS elem `conduct hotline told` cs
        `rescue and mitigation measures were not fully taken`             IS elem `conduct mitigation not taken` cs
        `the police or local authority were not told at once`             IS elem `conduct police not told` cs
        `the Insurer was not told at once`                                IS elem `conduct Insurer not told at once` cs
        `the Insurer's instructions were not followed`                    IS elem `conduct instructions not followed` cs
        `parked on a slope without brakes or chocks, so it rolled`        IS elem `conduct parked on a slope` cs
        `dismantled or repaired without the Insurer's approval`           IS elem `conduct dismantled without approval` cs
        `the Insurer gave no opinion within 5 working days of the notice` IS elem `conduct Insurer silent 5 working days` cs
        `the scene was not protected or the vehicle was moved from it`    IS elem `conduct scene not protected` cs
        `it was necessary for safety, to limit loss, or on an authority's order` IS elem `conduct necessary` cs
        `the Owner did not preserve and transfer the claim against the third party` IS elem `conduct claim against third party not preserved` cs
        `the Owner was untruthful in the claim documents`                 IS elem `conduct untruthful` cs
        `the use of the vehicle was misdeclared, so less premium was charged` IS elem `conduct use misdeclared` cs
        `an increase in risk was not notified`                            IS elem `conduct increase in risk not notified` cs
        `premium that should have been paid`                              IS `premium due`

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `A conduct in a test`
GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`the conduct where` cs MEANS
    `the conduct, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) `, premium that should have been paid` 12_000_000 `, where` cs

-- Prompt notice, on the day of the loss, and nothing else.
`good conduct` MEANS `the conduct where` EMPTY

§§ `The load and speed`

GIVEN `load` IS A NUMBER
      `persons with children` IS A NUMBER
      `persons without children` IS A NUMBER
      `speed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The load and speed`
`carrying` `load` `, persons counting children` `persons with children` `, not counting them` `persons without children` `, speed over the limit` `speed` MEANS
    `The load and speed` WITH
        `load carried`                                     IS `load`
        `persons carried, counting children under 7`       IS `persons with children`
        `persons carried, not counting children under 7`   IS `persons without children`
        `speed above the limit, by an authority's written conclusion` IS `speed`

`normal load` MEANS `carrying` 0 `, persons counting children` 2 `, not counting them` 2 `, speed over the limit` NOTHING

§§ `The damaged items`

DECLARE `An item fact in a test` IS ONE OF
    `item lost`
    `item same cause and time as other parts`
    `item wear or defect`
    `item indirect loss`
    `item consequential loss`
    `item engine water damage`
    `item accidental plunge`
    `item breakdown not from an insured peril`
    `item short circuit`
    `item caused by the modification`
    `item approved by the registry`
    `item cannot be repaired`

GIVEN k     IS A `A kind of part`
      how   IS A `How the item is put right`
      `repair cost` IS A NUMBER
      `new cost`    IS A NUMBER
      `used cost`   IS A NUMBER
      fs    IS A LIST OF `An item fact in a test`
      `agreed rate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`an item` k `put right by` how `, repair` `repair cost` `, new` `new cost` `, used` `used cost` `, facts` fs `, agreed rate` `agreed rate` MEANS
    `A damaged item` WITH
        `kind`                                                     IS k
        `put right by`                                             IS how
        `can be repaired`                                          IS NOT elem `item cannot be repaired` fs
        `reasonable cost of repair`                                IS `repair cost`
        `cost of a new replacement`                                IS `new cost`
        `cost of the used replacement part`                        IS `used cost`
        `lost`                                                     IS elem `item lost` fs
        `damaged or lost by the same cause and at the same time as other parts in the same accident` IS elem `item same cause and time as other parts` fs
        `wear and tear, inherent nature, defect, or damage in repair` IS elem `item wear or defect` fs
        `an indirect loss: lower commercial value, or loss tied to using the vehicle` IS elem `item indirect loss` fs
        `a consequential loss, as 12.23 defines it`                IS elem `item consequential loss` fs
        `engine damage from water: flood water or hydrolock`       IS elem `item engine water damage` fs
        `water entered after an accidental plunge into a pond, lake, river or stream` IS elem `item accidental plunge` fs
        `electrical or mechanical breakdown not caused by an insured peril` IS elem `item breakdown not from an insured peril` fs
        `electrical damage from overload, overpressure, short circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` IS elem `item short circuit` fs
        `the loss was caused by the added equipment or the modification` IS elem `item caused by the modification` fs
        `approved by the registry and within the inspection's validity` IS elem `item approved by the registry` fs
        `depreciation rate agreed at the assessment`                IS `agreed rate`

-- An ordinary part repaired for n.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a part repaired for` n MEANS
    `an item` `an ordinary part` `put right by` `repaired` `, repair` n `, new` (2 TIMES n) `, used` 0 `, facts` EMPTY `, agreed rate` NOTHING

-- A part of kind k that cannot be repaired, replaced with a new one costing n.
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of part`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a` k `replaced new for` n MEANS
    `an item` k `put right by` `replaced with a new part` `, repair` 0 `, new` n `, used` 0 `, facts` (LIST `item cannot be repaired`) `, agreed rate` NOTHING

-- An ordinary part of kind k, repaired for n, with the item facts fs.
GIVEN k  IS A `A kind of part`
      n  IS A NUMBER
      fs IS A LIST OF `An item fact in a test`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a` k `repaired for` n `where` fs MEANS
    `an item` k `put right by` `repaired` `, repair` n `, new` (2 TIMES n) `, used` 0 `, facts` fs `, agreed rate` NOTHING

§§ `The loss`

GIVEN `the date`  IS A DATE
      `the peril` IS A `A peril`
      c        IS A `The circumstances of the loss`
      ls       IS A `The load and speed`
      cd       IS A `The conduct after the loss`
      `the items` IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a loss on` `the date` `by` `the peril` `, circumstances` c `, load` ls `, conduct` cd `, items` `the items` MEANS
    `The loss` WITH
        `date of the loss`                                          IS `the date`
        `peril`                                                     IS `the peril`
        `sudden and unforeseeable`                                  IS TRUE
        `circumstances`                                             IS c
        `load and speed`                                            IS ls
        `conduct`                                                   IS cd
        `items`                                                     IS `the items`
        `share of the painted area damaged`                         IS 0
        `cost of repainting the damaged panels`                     IS 0
        `cost of repainting the whole vehicle`                      IS 0
        `cost of protecting the scene and preventing further loss`  IS 0
        `cost of rescue and transport to the nearest repair shop`   IS 0
        `the costs were incurred at the Insurer's request and direction` IS FALSE
        `market value immediately before the loss`                  IS 600_000_000
        `assessed damage`                                           IS 10_000_000
        `assessed cost of repair`                                   IS 10_000_000
        `a court judgment, or a decision to suspend the investigation or not to prosecute` IS FALSE
        `the Owner asks to keep the wreck`                          IS FALSE
        `value of the wreck, as valued`                             IS 0

-- A collision on Wednesday 10 June 2026, with the given circumstances and items.
GIVEN c  IS A `The circumstances of the loss`
      `the items` IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a collision with` c `, items` `the items` MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, circumstances` c `, load` `normal load` `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` `the items`

-- The plain collision: one ordinary part repaired for 10,000,000, nothing amiss.
`the plain collision` MEANS `a collision with` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

-- A loss by peril p, otherwise plain.
GIVEN p  IS A `A peril`
      `the items` IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a loss by` p `, items` `the items` MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` p `, circumstances` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, load` `normal load` `, conduct` `good conduct` `, items` `the items`

-- A total-loss case: the assessed damage and repair cost, and the wreck.
GIVEN `damage`  IS A NUMBER
      `repair`  IS A NUMBER
      `market value before` IS A NUMBER
      `keeps wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wreck value` IS A NUMBER
      `the peril` IS A `A peril`
      `judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a loss assessed at` `damage` `, repair` `repair` `, market value before` `market value before` `, wreck kept` `keeps wreck` `at` `wreck value` `, by` `the peril` `, judgment` `judgment` MEANS
    `The loss` WITH
        `date of the loss`                                          IS YMD 2026 6 10
        `peril`                                                     IS `the peril`
        `sudden and unforeseeable`                                  IS TRUE
        `circumstances`                                             IS `the circumstances with` EMPTY
        `load and speed`                                            IS `normal load`
        `conduct`                                                   IS `good conduct`
        `items`                                                     IS EMPTY
        `share of the painted area damaged`                         IS 0
        `cost of repainting the damaged panels`                     IS 0
        `cost of repainting the whole vehicle`                      IS 0
        `cost of protecting the scene and preventing further loss`  IS 0
        `cost of rescue and transport to the nearest repair shop`   IS 0
        `the costs were incurred at the Insurer's request and direction` IS FALSE
        `market value immediately before the loss`                  IS `market value before`
        `assessed damage`                                           IS `damage`
        `assessed cost of repair`                                   IS `repair`
        `a court judgment, or a decision to suspend the investigation or not to prosecute` IS `judgment`
        `the Owner asks to keep the wreck`                          IS `keeps wreck`
        `value of the wreck, as valued`                             IS `wreck value`

§§ `The claim`

`no earlier claims` MEANS `The earlier claims in the period` WITH
    `indemnity already paid under BS04 in the period`    IS 0
    `parts losses already paid under BS05 in the period` IS 0

`no journey costs` MEANS `The safe-journey costs` WITH
    `the vehicle could not move or be driven safely`                                       IS FALSE
    `cost of overnight stay and transport to the destination for the driver and occupants` IS 0
    `valid financial invoices were supplied`                                               IS FALSE

GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
      l IS A `The loss`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim on` p `for` l MEANS
    `The claim` WITH
        `policy`             IS p
        `loss`               IS l
        `earlier claims`     IS `no earlier claims`
        `safe-journey costs` IS `no journey costs`

GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
      l IS A `The loss`
      h IS A `The earlier claims in the period`
      j IS A `The safe-journey costs`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim on` p `for` l `, earlier` h `, journey` j MEANS
    `The claim` WITH
        `policy`             IS p
        `loss`               IS l
        `earlier claims`     IS h
        `safe-journey costs` IS j

§§ `Non-working days`

-- A HYPOTHETICAL calendar for the tests: the Saturdays and Sundays from June to October 2026,
-- and no public holiday. It is a test value, not a statement of which days are working days in
-- Vietnam (the rules do not say: fork F8).
`the test calendar` MEANS
    LIST (YMD 2026 6 6),  (YMD 2026 6 7),  (YMD 2026 6 13), (YMD 2026 6 14), (YMD 2026 6 20), (YMD 2026 6 21),
         (YMD 2026 6 27), (YMD 2026 6 28), (YMD 2026 7 4),  (YMD 2026 7 5),  (YMD 2026 7 11), (YMD 2026 7 12),
         (YMD 2026 7 18), (YMD 2026 7 19), (YMD 2026 7 25), (YMD 2026 7 26), (YMD 2026 8 1),  (YMD 2026 8 2),
         (YMD 2026 10 3), (YMD 2026 10 4), (YMD 2026 10 10), (YMD 2026 10 11), (YMD 2026 10 17), (YMD 2026 10 18)
